{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K1RCJKJsdstJVRWFqwwcbv","type":"tool_result","content":"9:## 0. At a glance\n35:### 0.1 Where each TASK.md requirement is covered\n70:## 1. The source: what to capture, what not to copy\n72:### 1.1 What research confirmed about Big Buck Hunter Pro\n99:### 1.2 Distinctive elements, turned into our mechanics\n114:### 1.3 Additions that make it a better game\n121:### 1.4 Do not copy\n130:## 2. Look, sound and tone\n162:## 3. Setup, folders and build\n164:### 3.1 Getting the engine and the hub client\n182:### 3.2 Environment notes (this machine)\n192:### 3.3 Dev folder layout\n214:### 3.4 Game source files (order = load order)\n251:### 3.5 The bundle\n284:## 4. Architecture\n286:### 4.1 The stack\n304:### 4.2 Conventions\n326:### 4.3 Scenes and flow\n356:### 4.4 The frame\n367:### 4.5 The test handle\n374:## 5. Systems\n378:### 5.1 Lens and the camera director (`vista.js`: `E.Lens`; `32-site.js`: Director)\n407:### 5.2 Terrain (`vista.js`: `E.Heightfield`)\n443:### 5.3 The renderer (`vista.js`: `E.Vista`)\n503:### 5.4 Four-legged rigs (`quadruped.js`: `E.Quadruped`)\n579:### 5.5 Critters, people and other rigs\n592:### 5.6 Animal AI (`30-actors.js`, `31-patterns.js`)\n642:### 5.7 Sites (`32-site.js`)\n681:### 5.8 Rifle, scope and call (`40-weapon.js`) and aiming (`41-aim.js`)\n721:### 5.9 Shot resolution and hit zones (`42-shot.js`)\n766:### 5.10 Scoring (`43-score.js`)\n794:### 5.11 Players and local multiplayer (`50-players.js`)\n808:### 5.12 HUD, prompts and glyphs (`51-hud.js`, `52-glyphs.js`)\n842:### 5.13 Feedback and juice\n856:### 5.14 Tally and the Shot Chart (`60-tally.js`)\n867:### 5.15 Trophy encounters (`61-trophy.js`)\n874:### 5.16 Bonus games (`62-bonus.js`)\n881:### 5.17 Modes and menus (`90-title.js`, `91-menu.js`, `92-hunt.js`, `94-about.js`, `53-ui.js`)\n904:### 5.18 The Lodge, records and saves (`93-lodge.js`)\n917:### 5.19 Dialog, barks and voices (`71-barks.js`, `babble.js`)\n930:### 5.20 Audio (`70-audio.js`)\n957:### 5.21 Attract mode and the HunterBot (`95-attract.js`)\n978:### 5.22 Dev mode (`96-dev.js`)\n1003:### 5.23 Settings and accessibility\n1010:### 5.24 Input map and game options (`01-game.js`)\n1036:### 5.25 Touch-only devices\n1044:### 5.26 AI Hub (`97-hub.js`): ghost mode\n1089:### 5.27 About & Credits and the reports (`94-about.js`)\n1099:## 6. Content\n1101:### 6.1 Hunts and maps\n1112:### 6.2 Sites\n1130:### 6.3 Trophies\n1138:### 6.4 Bonus games (30 s each)\n1148:### 6.5 Practice Range (Uncle Dub's)\n1161:### 6.6 Species (gameplay numbers)\n1169:### 6.7 Critters (12 designs)\n1186:### 6.8 Cast and story beats\n1207:### 6.9 Barks (emcee unless noted)\n1226:### 6.10 Items and unlockables\n1238:## 7. Build order and milestones\n1264:## 8. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1282:## 9. Testing\n1284:### 9.1 One command\n1298:### 9.2 Suites (headless)\n1322:### 9.3 Browser checks (`--browser`, Playwright, Chromium from the cache, `TMPDIR` set)\n1334:### 9.4 AI Hub harness (`--hub`)\n1341:### 9.5 Balance (`--balance`)\n1349:## 10. Definition of done (from TASK.md)\n1368:## Appendix A. Dev sliders (defaults)\n1396:## Appendix B. Data shapes\n1417:## Appendix C. Engine changes (keep this list; it goes in the Engine Feedback)\n1431:## Appendix D. `game.debug` and the snapshot\n1446:## Appendix E. The reports: Source Information, feedback, the exit interview\n1453:### E.1 Source Information\n1472:### E.2 Feedback\n1480:### E.3 exit-interview.json\n1547:## Appendix F. Research sources\nengine\nhub\nscripts\nAI_GUIDE.md\nAPI-INDEX.md\nAPI.md\nREADME.md\ndocs\ngame\nindex.html\nkits\nmodules\nmy-3d2dge-agent.js\nmy-3d2dge.js\npackage.json\nsrc\ntools","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e576ea7-ae6c-4602-b536-6bfa64a9b891","uuid":"2576c350-5c04-4321-94dc-794acaebab16","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:38:21.509Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"9:## 0. At a glance\n35:### 0.1 Where each TASK.md requirement is covered\n70