{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TTvvj2Qio7Ur9Ax8KN7q54","type":"tool_result","content":"chromium-1243\nchromium_headless_shell-1243\nffmpeg-1011\nfirefox-1543\nwebkit-2359\nv24.22.1\nls: cannot access '/home/micha/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research/engine/dist/handoff/node_modules': No such file or directory\nasset-find.mjs\nasset-lib.mjs\nasset-set.mjs\nasset-sheet.mjs\ncheck.mjs\nfilmstrip.mjs\nreplay.mjs\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' } (the world point it meets) or null off the map. Cells only, as height() has them (not props, actors, or walls cut away)\n39:const E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\n88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n94:- 1338 Module fight: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training (engine/modules/fight.js); E.FightAI: fightai, E.FightSelect: fightselect, E.FightStage: fightstage, E.Fighter: fighter, E.Match: match\n183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }); Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, COIN) (depth sorted) or px.sprite(g, COIN, sx, sy).\n215:- `E.anim(frames, fps = 8, o = {})` †: frames to play: anim([spr1, spr2, spr3], fps = 8, { loop: true, pingpong: false }), or anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 }) for several frames side by side in one sprite's rows. Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, a, { t }) (t: its clock, seconds; the game's time by default); a.frame(t) is the sprite at time t, a.index(t) its number, a.duration one play (seconds)\n250:- `game.screen.clientToScreen(cx, cy)`: browser client coords -> projected screen pixels (same space as view.p)\n266:- `game.screen.scale = 'auto'`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' (whole-number scale, every pixel the same size, black bars unless o.expand grows the picture into them), 'fill' (the largest fit, pixels a device pixel apart in size) or 'auto' (fill on high-density screens, phones and tablets, where that difference can't be seen; sharp elsewhere). game.settings.scale sets it\n289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses, double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point\n309:- `input.screenPoint(cx, cy)` †: browser client coords -> screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space, with no camera), or null without a canvas\n455:- `new E.Game({ expand })`: true makes res the least the screen shows and grows the picture to fill the window, any shape, no bars (expand: { maxW, maxH } stops it growing there)\n501:- `game.splitScreen(n, o = {})` †: split the screen into n viewports (2 to 4; 0 or 1: one screen again), o: { layout: 'auto' (side by side on a wide screen, stacked on a tall one; a grid for 3 or 4) | 'columns' | 'rows' | 'grid', follow: [targets], z: 16, gap: 1 }\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n571:- `fullscreen.enter(quiet)`: go full screen. Browsers allow it only from a tap, click or key press: call it from one (a button, the menu, a key's update step). Returns a promise of whether it worked (a refusal is kept in failed and noted on screen, unless quiet)\n574:- `fullscreen.standalone`: true when the page was opened from a home screen as an app (no browser bars: nothing to go full screen from)\n582:- `E.diagnose(game = E.current)`: the report a bug needs, at any time (and on the boot screen when a game can't start): { engine, game, time, page, browser, device, screen, canvas, gpu, sound, storage, input, scene, errors, text (all of it, one line each, for a screenshot or a bug report), short (one line) }. game: the game to report on (E.current)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n733:- `new E.TileMap(o = {}) → map`: Walls standing on a floor (top-down, isometric, brawler). Either { rows: [...ASCII...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types, floorTex } (recommended) or { w, h, cells: [ids...], floor: [tags...], blocked: [0 | 1...], types, floorTex } (built in code: fill, setFloor; with no cells it starts as open floor).\n741:- `map.arcClear(a, b, apex = 20, r = 0)`: does a jump arc from a to b (feet, { x, y, z }) clear every top on the way? The arc is a parabola peaking apex above the higher end; r > 0 also checks a track on each side of it. Jumps, throws, aerial takedowns","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e576ea7-ae6c-4602-b536-6bfa64a9b891","uuid":"1528f9b7-8790-4086-b94c-42ed2d32877e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:39:07.031Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"chromium-1243\nchromium_headless_shell-1243\nffmpeg-1011\nfirefox-1543\nwebkit-2359\nv24.22.1\nls: cannot access '/home/micha/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research/engine/dist/handoff/node_modules': No such file or directory\nasset-find.mjs\nasset-lib.mjs\nasset-set.mjs\nasset-sheet.mjs\ncheck.mjs\nfilmstrip.mjs\nreplay.mjs\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' } (the world point it meets) or null off the map. Cells only, as height() has them (not props, actors, or walls cut away)\n39:const E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\n88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n94:- 