{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghuRy69qiT7bENJoh9xs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0163WHauh6uFRARA1pYke7WD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-053803__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHuntOff*/; sed -n 200,240p ../../../../../../../../../home/micha/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research/engine/dist/handoff/API.md | cut -c1-900"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8915,"cache_read_input_tokens":103504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8915},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e576ea7-ae6c-4602-b536-6bfa64a9b891","uuid":"5a082ccc-2869-434c-86e2-5ae8ed2885a4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:41:18.618Z","request_id":"req_011CghuRxqHH4gJ8viFgEj2g","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0163WHauh6uFRARA1pYke7WD":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-053803__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHuntOff*/; sed -n 200,240p ../../../../../../../../../home/micha/.cache/x2e02c0-plan-research/engine/dist/handoff/API.md | cut -c1-900"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0163WHauh6uFRARA1pYke7WD","type":"tool_result","content":"## Characters\n**Humanoid** (knights, heroes, soldiers, zombies): `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'chibi' (default) | 'heroic' (tall, SotN) | 'bulky' (brawlers, bosses) | 'skeleton' (rib cage, skull, glowing eye sockets; tint with colors.bone), weapon: 'sword' (the default) | 'gun' | 'staff' | null (fists), outfit: 'shirt' | 'tunic' | 'robe' | 'coat', hair: 'short' | 'spiky' | 'long' | 'ponytail' | 'bald', hat: 'cap' | 'pointed' | 'helmet' | 'band' | 'crown' (or { style, color }), sleeves: 'short' | 'long' | 'none', armor, hood (in colors.hair), cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.5 }, eyeGlow, hunch, lean, style: 'hd' (default) | 'classic' (stick figures for huge crowds), colors: { skin, hair, cloth, coat, pants, boot, belt, trim, glove, cape, capeIn, metal, plate, hilt, eye, iris } })` (`metal` colors the weapon, `plate` the armor, defaulting to `metal`).\n- `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, air, point, aim, attack })`. `facing` is an angle (side view: 0 = right, `Math.PI` = left). `air: true` tucks the legs for jumps; `point: true` holds a gun forward; `aim` tilts it (radians, + = up: `aim: .8` shoots diagonally up, `Math.PI / 2` straight up).\n- **Moves** (`E.MOVES`, use them instead of hand-made specs; every one has anticipation, a committed strike with lunge / step / lean / twist, follow-through and a clean return to the stance, on every build and in every view):\n  - blades and clubs: `slash backslash overhead rising thrust spin plunge twohand`;\n  - fists: `jab` (left hand) `cross hook uppercut haymaker elbow`;\n  - kicks: `kick roundhouse sweep flyingkick knee axekick`;\n  - other: `cast` (both hands) `throw bash claw`.\n  Give each character its own set (a knight: `overhead`, `thrust`, `spin`; a mage: `cast`; a monk: `jab`, `cross`, `roundhouse`; a boss: `haymaker`, `sweep`). `E.move('uppercut', .5)` is the attack state of any move at any moment (previews, cutscenes).\n- `attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }`, spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, r0, r1, hand, rel, blade, spin, kick, plane, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`. Angles are relative to facing (+ = right hand side). `rel: true`: heights relative to the shoulder and reach scaled by arm length (kick heights as a share of hip height). `r0`/`r1`: reach that extends (thrusts, jabs). `hand: 'L' | 'both'`. In side views horizontal swings turn into the screen plane (a Castlevania chop) by themselves; `plane: 'side' | 'ground'` (or the rig option `swingPlane`) chooses. `lunge` steps into the strike (body motion in local units, clamped to -4..5; to move the character itself, add speed to your body), `hop` lifts the body, `crouch` dips in the wind-up, `hold` is how long the end pose holds (share of recover). You time the phases.\n- In steep ground views (threequarter) rigs and Blobs are drawn from a lower, sprite-like angle so faces show, like SNES RPG sprites (`charView: false` turns it off for one rig, `E.style.charPitch = false` for all).\n- Faces (eyes with catch-lights, brows, mouth), a cheated 3/4 turn toward the camera in side views (`cheat: .5`, 0 turns it off) and hair layers are automatic. `face: { eyes: 'big' (anime / Mana style), bangs: 0..1 }`.\n- Poses: `rig.update(dt, { ..., pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' })` (victory with the weapon raised, spell casting, a boxer's guard, hurt or resting, ducking, greeting, a cocky idle, knocked out; they blend in and out), `'block'` (weapon held upright across the body), `'die'` (a stagger, the knees give, then the body topples), `expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince'` (faces and portraits), `run: 0..1` (run in place), or `down: 0..1` to lie a defeated body flat (centred on its position). `stance: 'guard'` keeps fists up while walking (brawlers; the free hand guards the chin during punches), `stance: 'ready'` holds the weapon forward. `climb: true` with `vz` climbs a ladder hand over hand (`Platformer.rigState()` passes both). Traversal: `crouch` (a sneaking gait), `sprint` (a lean), `hang` with `hangZ` (hands on an edge that high above\n- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)` inside `r.actor`, `rig.drawSmear(r)` (a glowing trail along the real blade, fist or foot path, in every view), `rig.debug(r)` (skeleton), `rig.kick(v)` (squash and stretch), `rig.hand()` and `rig.tip()` (world points to spawn bullets from), `rig.worldOffset(p)` (where a point in the rig's own frame, such as a joint in `rig.J`, sits from its feet: to draw or spawn at any joint), `rig.lastView` (the view it last drew with), `rig.solvePose()` (sets `rig.J` from its state each step: wrap it on one rig to move joints).\n**Blob** (slimes, rabbites, bats, imps, round monsters): `new E.Blob({ R: 6, colors: { dk, base, lt, spec, eye, pupil }, ears: 'rabbit' | 'cat', horns: true, wings: true, feet: true, tail: true, mouth: true | 'fangs', face: 'front' })`, `update(dt, { squash: -0.4..0.4, look: [dx, dy], squint, walk: 0..1, flap: 0..1 (wing speed; 0 folds them), hang: true (roost upside down) })`, `kick(v)`, `draw(g, ox, oy, view)`. Mix the parts for a bestiary: `wings` + `mouth: 'fangs'` is a bat, `ears: 'rabbit'` + `feet` a Mana rabbite, `horns` + `tail` an imp.\n\n## Effects and lighting\n- Particles: `game.particles.explosion(x, y, z, size)` (fireball, smoke, sparks, debris, ring, shake, sound), `fire(x, y, z, n, { size })`, `smoke(x, y, z, n, { size, color })`, `glints(x, y, z, n, color)`, `dust(x, y, z, n)`, `sparks(x, y, z, n, angle)`, `bits(x, y, z, n, colors)`, `ring(x, y, r0, r1, color, dur)`, `text(x, y, z, '12', color, { scale: 2, bounce: true })` (bouncing damage numbers), `add({ kind: 'dust' | 'spark' | 'bit' | 'ember' | 'fire' | 'smoke' | 'glint', ... })`. `explosion(x, y, z, size, { debris, freeze: false, shake: 0 })` for chains of small blasts. Side-scrollers: `particles.ground = (x, y, z) => level.groundBelow(x, z)` so sparks and debris bounce on platforms. Screen flash: `game.flash('#ffffff', .12, strength 0..1)`.\n- Lighting (step 9; every view, side-scrollers included, no WebGPU needed): `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity, { color: '#ffa050' })` every draw. Dark areas get a smooth cool tint, lights add their own color, and emissive items (flames, sparks, bullets, `emissive: true`) stay bright. `lights.darkness` (0..1) and `lights.tint` tune it; after setting `lights.dark = [r, g, b]`, `levels` or `glow`, call `lights.refresh()`. Props with flames can light the scene: `r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { light: true })`. Lamps, street lamps, lanterns and crystals glow on their own (`haloR`, `haloColor`, `halo: false`); `cone: true` adds a light cone under a street lamp.\n- Hits: `game.hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage: 12, textScale: 2, textZ: 22 })` does hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks, a bouncing damage number (`bounce: false` floats it) and a sound in one call; `particles.impact(x, y, z, size, color)` for the star alone.\n- GPU lighting (optional, ground views with a TileMap): `const gpu = game.enableGPU({ map })`; mark glowing things with `px.glow(g, 1)`; add `lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` and `lights.heat(x, y, z, w)`. Where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with `game.lights.ambient` (`gpu.fallback = false`: unlit).\n\n## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n| Genre (examples) | View | Build it with | Copy slice |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Platformer (Mario, Mega Man, Sonic, Castlevania) | `side` (+ `brawler` for 2.5D) | PlatformMap, Platformer, Humanoid, sprites, Bullets `'side'` | PLATFORMER |\n| Metroidvania (Metroid, Symphony of the Night) | `side` | an `E.World` of PlatformMaps (the rooms module: doors at open edges, a slide, the explored map, gates opened by abilities, saves), a Platformer given `airJumps` and `dash` as they are found, its further moves, an arm cannon aimed eight ways (`point`, `aim`, `rig.tip()`, Bullets) | METROIDVANIA |\n| Action adventure (Zelda, Secret of Mana) | `threequarter` or `topdown` | TileMap rows, `cam.room`, Body, Humanoid + `E.Attack` sword, Dialog, `E.ui.hearts` | ADVENTURE |\n| Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword) | none: rooms painted in screen pixels (`r.overlay`) | `E.Click` (the click module): rooms with walk areas and holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots, the nine verbs, Sierra's icons or a verb coin, an inventory, puzzles as rules; talk through `E.Story` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad) | none | `E.Story` nodes and choices over a painted backdrop, `rig.drawPortrait` at size, `story.log` (the backlog), `story.auto`, `story.skip`; `game.saves` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Action RPG / dungeon (Diablo, Landstalker) | `iso` | TileMap, FlowField, Body (jump onto blocks), GPU lighting | ADVENTURE |\n| Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage, TMNT) | `brawler` | TileMap street strip, Body, Humanoid (`weapon: null`) + `E.Combo` punches and `kick: true` kicks, `E.knockback`, waves that lock the screen; a second player drops in (`game.allowJoin`, `cam.frame` on both) | BRAWLER |\n| Fighting (Street Fighter II, Darkstalkers) | `side` | two `E.Fighter`s in an `E.Match` (the fight module): moves with frame data, guards, throws, specials by motion (`'236'`) or charge, a meter, projectiles; `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`, training | FIGHTING |\n| Shoot-'em-up (1942, Gradius, R-Type) | `overhead` (vertical, and horizontal: world x scrolls) | sprites, Bullets, `E.pattern`, a timeline of waves; horizontal: rock edges as functions of x, a power bar, options on the ship's past path, `E.Path` loops; `E.Arcade` for the continue and the table | SHOOTER (both stages) |\n| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\n| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\n| Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids) | `overhead` (one fixed screen, cabinet art on the sides) | `E.Arcade` (score, lives, extra lives, turns, initials, tables, attract mode); a maze of `E.GridMover`s; moths on `E.Path`s turned by `rot`; `E.wrap` and `wrap: [w, h]` | ARCADE |\n| Twin-stick / run-and-gun (Smash TV, Contra) | `topdown` / `side` | Body or Platformer, Bullets, `weapon: 'gun'`, `point: true` | SHOOTER + ADVENTURE |\n| JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, EarthBound) | `threequarter` town, `brawler` battles | TileMap towns and a big world map, the story and rpg modules, Dialog with markup, `game.saves` slots | RPG |\n| Puzzle (Tetris, Dr. Mario, Puyo, Columns) | `side` (a field in screen pixels) | a cell array, a bag from `E.rng`, `input.repeat` (auto-shift), `grid.groups` (chains), `input.drag()` and `clicked()` for touch; versus: two fields, rows sent across (`game.players`) | PUZZLE |\n| Roguelike (Rogue, Mystery Dungeon, Shiren) | `threequarter` / `iso` | `E.gen` floors, a TileMap of its rows, `E.Grid.from(map)` paths and `fov`, `E.Fog`, `E.Turns` by speed, `game.tween` steps | ROGUELIKE |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e576ea7-ae6c-4602-b536-6bfa64a9b891","uuid":"0e3f9387-d6c5-4307-967a-99f5ff3ca7e4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:41:18.641Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Characters\n**Humanoid** (knights, heroes, soldiers, zombies): `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build: 'chibi' (default) | 'heroic' (tall, SotN) | 'bulky' (brawlers, bosses) | 'skeleton' (rib cage, skull, glowing eye sockets; tint with colors.bone), weapon: 'sword' (the default) | 'gun' | 'staff' | null (fists), outfit: 'shirt' | 'tunic' | 'robe' | 'coat', hair: 'short' | 'spiky' | 'long' | 'ponytail' | 'bald', hat: 'cap' | 'pointed' | 'helmet' | 'band' | 'crown' (or { style, color }), sleeves: 'short' | 'long' | 'none', armor, hood (in colors.hair), cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.5 }, eyeGlow, hunch, lean, style: 'hd' (default) | 'classic' (stick figures for huge crowds), colors: { skin, hair, cloth, coat, pants, boot, belt, trim, glove, cape, capeIn, metal, plate, hilt, eye, iris } })` (`metal` colors the weapon, `plate` the armor, defaulting to `metal`).\n- `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, air, point, aim, attack })`. `facing` is an angle (side view: 0 = right, `Math.PI` = left). `air: true` tucks the legs for jumps; `point: true` holds a gun forward; `aim` tilts it (radians, + = up: `aim: .8` shoots diagonally up, `Math.PI / 2` straight up).\n- **Moves** (`E.MOVES`, use them instead of hand-made specs; every one has anticipation, a committed strike with lunge / step / lean / twist, follow-through and a clean return to the stance, on every build and in every view):\n  - blades and clubs: `slash backslash overhead rising thrust spin plunge twohand`;\n  - fists: `jab` (left hand) `cross hook uppercut haymaker elbow`;\n  - kicks: `kick roundhouse sweep flyingkick knee axekick`;\n  - other: `cast` (both hands) `throw bash claw`.\n  Give each character its own set (a knight: `overhead`, `thrust`, `spin`; a mage: `cast`; a monk: `jab`, `cross`, `roundhouse`; a boss: `haymaker`, `sweep`). `E.move('uppercut', .5)` is the attack state of any move at any moment (previews, cutscenes).\n- `attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }`, spec `{ a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, r0, r1, hand, rel, blade, spin, kick, plane, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`. Angles are relative to facing (+ = right hand side). `rel: true`: heights relative to the shoulder and reach scaled by arm length (kick heights as a share of hip height). `r0`/`r1`: reach that extends (thrusts, jabs). `hand: 'L' | 'both'`. In side views horizontal swings turn into the screen plane (a Castlevania chop) by themselves; `plane: 'side' | 'ground'` (or the rig option `swingPlane`) chooses. `lunge` steps into the strike (body motion in local units, clamped to -4..5; to move the character itself, add speed to your body), `hop` lifts the body, `crouch` dips in the wind-up, `hold` is how long the end pose holds (share of recover). You time the phases.\n- In steep ground views (threequarter) rigs and Blobs are drawn from a lower, sprite-like angle so faces show, like SNES RPG sprites (`charView: false` turns it off for one rig, `E.style.charPitch = false` for all).\n- Faces (eyes with catch-lights, brows, mouth), a cheated 3/4 turn toward the camera in side views (`cheat: .5`, 0 turns it off) and hair layers are automatic. `face: { eyes: 'big' (anime / Mana style), bangs: 0..1 }`.\n- Poses: `rig.update(dt, { ..., pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' })` (victory with the weapon raised, spell casting, a boxer's guard, hurt or resting, ducking, greeting, a cocky idle, knocked out; they blend in and out), `'block'` (weapon held upright across the body), `'die'` (a stagger, the knees give, then the body topples), `expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince'` (faces and portraits), `run: 0..1` (run in place), or `down: 0..1` to lie a defeated body flat (centred on its position). `stance: 'guard'` keeps fists up while walking (brawlers; the free hand guards the chin during punches), `stance: 'ready'` holds the weapon forward. `climb: true` with `vz` climbs a ladder hand over hand (`Platformer.rigState()` passes both). Traversal: `crouch` (a sneaking gait), `sprint` (a lean), `hang` with `hangZ` (hands on an edge that high above\n- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)` inside `r.actor`, `rig.drawSmear(r)` (a glowing trail along the real blade, fist or foot path, in every view), `rig.debug(r)` (skeleton), `rig.kick(v)` (squash and stretch), `rig.hand()` and `rig.tip()` (world points to spawn bullets from), `rig.worldOffset(p)` (where a point in the rig's own frame, such as a joint in `rig.J`, sits from its feet: to draw or spawn at any joint), `rig.lastView` (the view it last drew with), `rig.solvePose()` (sets `rig.J` from its state each step: wrap it on one rig to move joints).\n**Blob** (slimes, rabbites, bats, imps, round monsters): `new E.Blob({ R: 6, colors: { dk, base, lt, spec, eye, pupil }, ears: 'rabbit' | 'cat', horns: true, wings: true, feet: true, tail: true, mouth: true | 'fangs', face: 'front' })`, `update(dt, { squash: -0.4..0.4, look: [dx, dy], squint, walk: 0..1, flap: 0..1 (wing speed; 0 folds them), hang: true (roost upside down) })`, `kick(v)`, `draw(g, ox, oy, view)`. Mix the parts for a bestiary: `wings` + `mouth: 'fangs'` is a bat, `ears: 'rabbit'` + `feet` a Mana rabbite, `horns` + `tail` an imp.\n\n## Effects and lighting\n- Particles: `game.particles.explosion(x, y, z, size)` (fireball, smoke, sparks, debris, ring, shake, sound), `fire(x, y, z, n, { size })`, `smoke(x, y, z, n, { size, color })`, `glints(x, y, z, n, color)`, `dust(x, y, z, n)`, `sparks(x, y, z, n, angle)`, `bits(x, y, z, n, colors)`, `ring(x, y, r0, r1, color, dur)`, `text(x, y, z, '12', color, { scale: 2, bounce: true })` (bouncing damage numbers), `add({ kind: 'dust' | 'spark' | 'bit' | 'ember' | 'fire' | 'smoke' | 'glint', ... })`. `explosion(x, y, z, size, { debris, freeze: false, shake: 0 })` for chains of small blasts. Side-scrollers: `particles.ground = (x, y, z) => level.groundBelow(x, z)` so sparks and debris bounce on platforms. Screen flash: `game.flash('#ffffff', .12, strength 0..1)`.\n- Lighting (step 9; every view, side-scrollers included, no WebGPU needed): `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity, { color: '#ffa050' })` every draw. Dark areas get a smooth cool tint, lights add their own color, and emissive items (flames, sparks, bullets, `emissive: true`) stay bright. `lights.darkness` (0..1) and `lights.tint` tune it; after setting `lights.dark = [r, g, b]`, `levels` or `glow`, call `lights.refresh()`. Props with flames can light the scene: `r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { light: true })`. Lamps, street lamps, lanterns and crystals glow on their own (`haloR`, `haloColor`, `halo: false`); `cone: true` adds a light cone under a street lamp.\n- Hits: `game.hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage: 12, textScale: 2, textZ: 22 })` does hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks, a bouncing damage number (`bounce: false` floats it) and a sound in one call; `particles.impact(x, y, z, size, color)` for the star alone.\n- GPU lighting (optional, ground views with a TileMap): `const gpu = game.enableGPU({ map })`; mark glowing things with `px.glow(g, 1)`; add `lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` and `lights.heat(x, y, z, w)`. Where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with `game.lights.ambient` (`gpu.fallback = false`: unlit).\n\n## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n| Genre (examples) | View | Build it with | Copy slice |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Platformer (Mario, Mega Man, Sonic, Castlevania) | `side` (+ `brawler` for 2.5D) | PlatformMap, Platformer, Humanoid, sprites, Bullets `'side'` | PLATFORMER |\n| Metroidvania (Metroid, Symphony of the Night) | `side` | an `E.World` of PlatformMaps (the rooms module: doors at open edges, a slide, the explored map, gates opened by abilities, saves), a Platformer given `airJumps` and `dash` as they are found, its further moves, an arm cannon aimed eight ways (`point`, `aim`, `rig.tip()`, Bullets) | METROIDVANIA |\n| Action adventure (Zelda, Secret of Mana) | `threequarter` or `topdown` | TileMap rows, `cam.room`, Body, Humanoid + `E.Attack` sword, Dialog, `E.ui.hearts` | ADVENTURE |\n| Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword) | none: rooms painted in screen pixels (`r.overlay`) | `E.Click` (the click module): rooms with walk areas and holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots, the nine verbs, Sierra's icons or a verb coin, an inventory, puzzles as rules; talk through `E.Story` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad) | none | `E.Story` nodes and choices over a painted backdrop, `rig.drawPortrait` at size, `story.log` (the backlog), `story.auto`, `story.skip`; `game.saves` | POINT-AND-CLICK |\n| Action RPG / dungeon (Diablo, Landstalker) | `iso` | TileMap, FlowField, Body (jump onto blocks), GPU lighting | ADVENTURE |\n| Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage, TMNT) | `brawler` | TileMap street strip, Body, Humanoid (`weapon: null`) + `E.Combo` punches and `kick: true` kicks, `E.knockback`, waves that lock the screen; a second player drops in (`game.allowJoin`, `cam.frame` on both) | BRAWLER |\n| Fighting (Street Fighter II, Darkstalkers) | `side` | two `E.Fighter`s in an `E.Match` (the fight module): moves with frame data, guards, throws, specials by motion (`'236'`) or charge, a meter, projectiles; `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`, training | FIGHTING |\n| Shoot-'em-up (1942, Gradius, R-Type) | `overhead` (vertical, and horizontal: world x scrolls) | sprites, Bullets, `E.pattern`, a timeline of waves; horizontal: rock edges as functions of x, a power bar, options on the ship's past path, `E.Path` loops; `E.Arcade` for the continue and the table | SHOOTER (both stages) |\n| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\n| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\n| Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids) | `overhead` (one fixed screen, cabinet art on the sides) | `E.Arcade` (score, lives, extra lives, turns, initials, tables, attract mode); a maze of `E.GridMover`s; moths on `E.Path`s turned by `rot`; `E.wrap` and `wrap: [w, h]` | ARCADE |\n| Twin-stick / run-and-gun (Smash TV, Contra) | `topdown` / `side` | Body or Platformer, Bullets, `weapon: 'gun'`, `point: true` | SHOOTER + ADVENTURE |\n| JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, EarthBound) | `threequarter` town, `brawler` battles | TileMap towns and a big world map, the story and rpg modules, Dialog with markup, `game.saves` slots | RPG |\n| Puzzle (Tetris, Dr. Mario, Puyo, Columns) | `side` (a field in screen pixels) | a cell array, a bag from `E.rng`, `input.repeat` (auto-shift), `grid.groups` (chains), `input.drag()` and `clicked()` for touch; versus: two fields, rows sent across (`game.players`) | PUZZLE |\n| Roguelike (Rogue, Mystery Dungeon, Shiren) | `threequarter` / `iso` | `E.gen` floors, a TileMap of its rows, `E.Grid.from(map)` paths and `fov`, `E.Fog`, `E.Turns` by speed, `game.tween` steps | ROGUELIKE |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0163WHauh6uFRARA1pYke7WD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghuSSLFEKvYVHM8Cqmjc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5973,"cache_read_input_tokens":112419,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5973},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e576ea7-ae6c-4602-b536-6bfa64a9b891","uuid":"9574a519-3ac8-413e-81a1-5d9bb8c261f9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:41:24.147Z","request_id":"req_011CghuSRzf9sMH5zepUrGEu","thinking_duration_ms":999,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghuSSLFEKvYVHM8Cqmjc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Setup is done. Dev folder, engine and hub client are in place. Now I'm writing the game source, starting with the core, input and audio modules."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5973,"cache_read_input_tokens":112419,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5973},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e576ea7-ae6c-4602-b536-6bfa64a9b891","uuid":"324e6e60-a100-4a18-b0e2-4bc0801c89d5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:41:24.149Z","request_id":"req_011CghuSRzf9sMH5zepUrGEu"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghuSSLFEKvYVHM8Cqmjc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tcov1s4E3w1H9F68tsbRux","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-053803__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-053803/src/00-core.js","content":"/* BIG BUCK HUNT-OFF — core: constants, RNG streams, tuning, event bus, records, glyphs, input helpers.\n   CORE LOOP: spot the bucks, shoot clean, pump, never shoot a doe; bag them before they're gone, then read your shots\n   in x-ray and climb the standings. */\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst BB = globalThis.BB = { E, VERSION: '1.0' };\nconst clamp = (v, a, b) => v < a ? a : v > b ? b : v;\nconst lerp = (a, b, t) => a + (b - a) * t;\nBB.clamp = clamp; BB.lerp = lerp;\n\n/* ---------- seeded RNG streams (never Math.random in gameplay) ---------- */\nfunction mulberry(seed) {\n  let s = seed >>> 0;\n  const f = () => { s = (s + 0x6D2B79F5) >>> 0; let t = s; t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };\n  f.seed = seed; return f;\n}\nBB.rng = mulberry;\nconst hashStr = s => { let h = 2166136261; for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) { h ^= s.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); } return h >>> 0; };\nBB.hashStr = hashStr;\nBB.RNG = {\n  runSeed: 4141,\n  streams: {},\n  stream(name) { return this.streams[name] || (this.streams[name] = mulberry(hashStr(name) ^ this.runSeed)); },\n  reseed(seed) { this.runSeed = seed >>> 0; this.streams = {}; },\n  /* cosmetic stream: drawing from it never shifts gameplay */\n  fx() { return this.stream('fx'); }\n};\nBB.rand = (a, b, name = 'spawn') => a + (b - a) * BB.RNG.stream(name)();\nBB.fxr = (a = 0, b = 1) => a + (b - a) * BB.RNG.stream('fx')();\nBB.pickFrom = (list, name = 'spawn') => list[Math.floor(BB.RNG.stream(name)() * list.length) % list.length];\n\n/* value noise used by terrain, fog and clouds */\nfunction hash2(ix, iy, seed) { let h = (ix * 374761393 + iy * 668265263 + seed * 2147483647) | 0; h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 1274126177); return ((h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }\nfunction noise2(x, y, seed = 1) {\n  const ix = Math.floor(x), iy = Math.floor(y), fx = x - ix, fy = y - iy;\n  const sx = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx), sy = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy);\n  const a = hash2(ix, iy, seed), b = hash2(ix + 1, iy, seed), c = hash2(ix, iy + 1, seed), d = hash2(ix + 1, iy + 1, seed);\n  return lerp(lerp(a, b, sx), lerp(c, d, sx), sy);\n}\nBB.noise2 = noise2; BB.hash2 = hash2;\n\n/* ---------- tuning (the dev sliders, Appendix A of the plan) ---------- */\nconst TUNING_DEFS = [\n  ['animalSpeed', 'Animal speed', 1, .25, 2, .05], ['spook', 'Gunshot fear', 1, 0, 2, .05], ['doeShare', 'Does and fawns', 1, 0, 2, .1],\n  ['siteTime', 'Site time x', 1, .3, 3, .1], ['reticleSpeed', 'Reticle speed', 330, 150, 900, 10], ['assist', 'Aim assist friction', .65, 0, 1, .05],\n  ['rounds', 'Rounds in tube', 5, 1, 10, 1], ['rackTime', 'Pump time', .22, 0, .6, .02], ['reloadTime', 'Reload time', 1.25, .2, 3, .05],\n  ['scopeMag', 'Scope zoom', 3.5, 1.5, 6, .1], ['sway', 'Scope sway', 2.6, 0, 6, .1], ['breath', 'Hold breath (s)', 3, 1, 6, .25],\n  ['calls', 'Calls per site', 2, 0, 5, 1], ['callFreeze', 'Call freeze (s)', 1.4, 0, 4, .1], ['distanceSlope', 'Metres per +1 dist x', 75, 25, 200, 5],\n  ['heartMult', 'Heart shot x', 2, .5, 4, .1], ['headMult', 'Head shot x', 1.8, .5, 4, .1], ['lungMult', 'Lung shot x', 1.6, .5, 4, .1],\n  ['runningMult', 'Running shot x', 1.25, 1, 2, .05], ['antlerBoost', 'Antler size', 1.15, 1, 2, .05], ['animalScale', 'Animal size', 1.1, .8, 1.6, .05],\n  ['fog', 'Fog', 1, 0, 2, .1], ['timeOfDay', 'Time of day', 0, -1, 1, .1], ['timeScale', 'Game speed', 1, .1, 2, .05]\n];\nBB.TUNING_DEFS = TUNING_DEFS;\nBB.T = {};\nBB.dev = { god: false, infinite: false, freeze: false, slow: false, overlays: { zones: false, labels: false, fps: false }, open: false, page: 0, freecam: false };\nfunction resetTuning() { for (const d of TUNING_DEFS) BB.T[d[0]] = d[2]; }\nresetTuning();\nBB.resetTuning = () => { resetTuning(); saveTuning(); };\nfunction saveTuning() { try { E.store.set('bbho.tuning', BB.T); } catch (e) { /* storage blocked */ } }\nBB.saveTuning = saveTuning;\nBB.loadTuning = () => { const t = E.store.get('bbho.tuning', null); if (t) for (const d of TUNING_DEFS) if (typeof t[d[0]] === 'number') BB.T[d[0]] = clamp(t[d[0]], d[3], d[4]); };\n\n/* ---------- event bus ---------- */\nconst handlers = {};\nBB.bus = {\n  on(n, f) { (handlers[n] || (handlers[n] = [])).push(f); return () => { handlers[n] = handlers[n].filter(h => h !== f); }; },\n  emit(n, d) { const l = handlers[n]; if (l) for (const f of l.slice()) { try { f(d); } catch (e) { if (BB.game) BB.game.fail('event ' + n, e); } } },\n  clear() { for (const k in handlers) delete handlers[k]; }\n};\n\n/* ---------- records (saves) ---------- */\nconst REC_KEY = 'bbho.records';\nBB.defaultRecords = () => ({ stars: {}, best: {}, mounts: {}, plaques: {}, range: false, champion: false, tables: {}, hunts: 0, shots: 0, kills: 0, tutorial: {} });\nBB.records = BB.defaultRecords();\nBB.loadRecords = () => { const r = E.store.get(REC_KEY, null); if (r && typeof r === 'object') BB.records = Object.assign(BB.defaultRecords(), r); };\nBB.saveRecords = () => { try { E.store.set(REC_KEY, BB.records); } catch (e) { /* ignore */ } };\nBB.resetRecords = () => { BB.records = BB.defaultRecords(); BB.saveRecords(); };\nBB.addScore = (table, name, score) => {\n  const t = BB.records.tables[table] || (BB.records.tables[table] = []);\n  t.push({ name, score }); t.sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score); t.length = Math.min(t.length, 8); BB.saveRecords();\n  return t.findIndex(e => e.name === name && e.score === score);\n};\nBB.tablePlaces = (table, score) => { const t = BB.records.tables[table] || []; return t.filter(e => e.score > score).length; };\n\n/* ---------- players' seat colours (AI Hub) and reticle shapes ---------- */\nBB.COLORS = ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'];\nBB.SHAPES = ['circle', 'diamond', 'brackets', 'triangle'];\nBB.COLOR_NAMES = ['RED', 'BLUE', 'GREEN', 'GOLD'];\n\n/* ---------- ui text helpers ---------- */\nBB.txt = (g, s, x, y, c = '#fff', o = {}) => E.font.text(g, s, Math.round(x), Math.round(y), c, Object.assign({ shadow: '#000', outline: false }, o));\nBB.tw = (s, o) => E.font.width(s, o || {});\nBB.fmt = n => String(Math.round(n)).replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, ',');\n\n/* ---------- glyphs: what to show for an action, by the device used last ---------- */\nconst PS = { cross: ['✕', '#7aa7ff'], circle: ['○', '#ff7a7a'], square: ['□', '#ff9ad0'], triangle: ['△', '#7ae0a8'] };\nconst XB = { cross: ['A', '#6fd07a'], circle: ['B', '#ff6a6a'], square: ['X', '#6aa0ff'], triangle: ['Y', '#ffd24a'] };\nconst ACTIONS = {\n  confirm: { pad: 'cross', key: 'Enter', mouse: 'Click' },\n  cancel: { pad: 'circle', key: 'Esc', mouse: 'Esc' },\n  fire: { pad: 'R2', key: 'Space', mouse: 'Click' },\n  pump: { pad: 'square', key: 'R', mouse: 'R / Wheel' },\n  scope: { pad: 'L2', key: 'Q', mouse: 'Right click' },\n  breath: { pad: 'L1', key: 'Shift', mouse: 'Shift' },\n  call: { pad: 'triangle', key: 'E', mouse: 'E' },\n  start: { pad: 'Options', key: 'Enter', mouse: 'Click' },\n  pause: { pad: 'Options', key: 'Esc', mouse: 'Esc' },\n  move: { pad: 'L stick', key: 'WASD', mouse: 'Mouse' },\n  aim: { pad: 'L stick', key: 'WASD', mouse: 'Mouse' },\n  join: { pad: 'Options', key: 'Enter', mouse: 'Click' },\n  tab: { pad: 'L1 R1', key: 'Q E', mouse: 'Q E' },\n  next: { pad: 'R1', key: 'Tab', mouse: 'Tab' }\n};\nBB.ACTIONS = ACTIONS;\nBB.device = () => { const g = BB.game; if (!g) return 'keyboard'; const d = g.input.lastDevice; return d === 'gamepad' ? 'pad' : d === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : d === 'touch' ? 'key' : 'key'; };\nBB.xbox = () => !!(BB.game && BB.game.settings && BB.game.settings.glyphs === 'Xbox');\n/* label for an action under the current device, e.g. ✕ / A / Enter */\nBB.glyphLabel = (act, dev) => {\n  const a = ACTIONS[act] || { pad: act, key: act, mouse: act }; dev = dev || BB.device();\n  if (dev === 'pad') {\n    const p = a.pad; const m = BB.xbox() ? XB : PS;\n    if (m[p]) return m[p][0];\n    if (BB.xbox()) return ({ R2: 'RT', L2: 'LT', L1: 'LB', R1: 'RB', 'L1 R1': 'LB RB', Options: 'Menu' })[p] || p;\n    return p;\n  }\n  return dev === 'mouse' ? a.mouse : a.key;\n};\n/* draws a small button glyph and returns its width */\nBB.glyph = (g, act, x, y, dev) => {\n  dev = dev || BB.device(); const lab = BB.glyphLabel(act, dev); const a = ACTIONS[act] || {};\n  const m = BB.xbox() ? XB : PS; const col = dev === 'pad' && m[a.pad] ? m[a.pad][1] : '#e8e4ff';\n  const w = Math.max(11, BB.tw(lab) + 6);\n  if (dev === 'pad') {\n    const r = 6; E.px.disc(g, x + 6, y + 5, r, '#10131f'); E.px.disc(g, x + 6, y + 5, r - 1, '#242a44');\n    if (m[a.pad]) { drawPadSym(g, a.pad, x + 6, y + 5, col); return 13; }\n    E.px.rect(g, x, y, w, 11, '#10131f'); E.px.rect(g, x + 1, y + 1, w - 2, 9, '#2c3354'); BB.txt(g, lab, x + 3, y + 2, '#fff', { shadow: false }); return w;\n  }\n  E.px.rect(g, x, y, w, 11, '#0b0d16'); E.px.rect(g, x + 1, y + 1, w - 2, 8, '#d9d6ea'); E.px.rect(g, x + 1, y + 9, w - 2, 1, '#8b86a8');\n  BB.txt(g, lab, x + 3, y + 2, '#1a1730', { shadow: false });\n  return w;\n};\nfunction drawPadSym(g, sym, cx, cy, col) {\n  if (BB.xbox()) { const t = XB[sym][0]; BB.txt(g, t, cx - BB.tw(t) / 2 + .5, cy - 3, col, { shadow: false }); return; }\n  const px = E.px;\n  if (sym === 'cross') { px.line(g, cx - 3, cy - 3, cx + 3, cy + 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx - 3, cy + 3, cx + 3, cy - 3, col, 1); }\n  else if (sym === 'circle') { for (let a = 0; a < 16; a++) px.dot(g, Math.round(cx + Math.cos(a / 16 * 6.283) * 3.4), Math.round(cy + Math.sin(a / 16 * 6.283) * 3.4), col); }\n  else if (sym === 'square') { px.line(g, cx - 3, cy - 3, cx + 3, cy - 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx + 3, cy - 3, cx + 3, cy + 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx + 3, cy + 3, cx - 3, cy + 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx - 3, cy + 3, cx - 3, cy - 3, col, 1); }\n  else { px.line(g, cx, cy - 4, cx + 4, cy + 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx + 4, cy + 3, cx - 4, cy + 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx - 4, cy + 3, cx, cy - 4, col, 1); }\n}\n/* a prompt row: [glyph] LABEL  [glyph] LABEL ... centred or left aligned; items: [[action, label], ...] */\nBB.prompts = (g, items, x, y, align = 'center', dev) => {\n  let total = 0; const parts = items.map(([a, l]) => { const gw = Math.max(13, BB.tw(BB.glyphLabel(a, dev)) + 7); const w = gw + 3 + BB.tw(l); total += w + 10; return [a, l, gw, w]; });\n  total -= 10; let cx = align === 'center' ? x - total / 2 : align === 'right' ? x - total : x;\n  for (const [a, l, gw, w] of parts) { BB.glyph(g, a, Math.round(cx), y, dev); BB.txt(g, l, cx + gw + 3, y + 2, '#e8e4ff'); cx += w + 10; }\n};\n\n/* ---------- audio helper: sfx on an offset (valley echoes) ---------- */\nBB.sfx = (name, o) => { const a = BB.game && BB.game.audio; if (a && !BB.muteSfx) try { a.sfx(name, o); } catch (e) { /* audio blocked */ } };\nBB.sfxLater = (name, delay, o) => { if (BB.game) BB.game.after(delay, () => BB.sfx(name, o)); };\n})();\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5973,"cache_read_input_tokens":112419,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5973},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e576ea7-ae6c-4602-b536-6bfa64a9b891","uuid":"0838605b-8e8d-48b9-8d8c-617d2da5b749","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:41:56.962Z","request_id":"req_011CghuSRzf9sMH5zepUrGEu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Tcov1s4E3w1H9F68tsbRux":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-053803__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-053803/src/00-core.js","content":"/* BIG BUCK HUNT-OFF — core: constants, RNG streams, tuning, event bus, records, glyphs, input helpers.\n   CORE LOOP: spot the bucks, shoot clean, pump, never shoot a doe; bag them before they're gone, then read your shots\n   in x-ray and climb the standings. */\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst BB = globalThis.BB = { E, VERSION: '1.0' };\nconst clamp = (v, a, b) => v < a ? a : v > b ? b : v;\nconst lerp = (a, b, t) => a + (b - a) * t;\nBB.clamp = clamp; BB.lerp = lerp;\n\n/* ---------- seeded RNG streams (never Math.random in gameplay) ---------- */\nfunction mulberry(seed) {\n  let s = seed >>> 0;\n  const f = () => { s = (s + 0x6D2B79F5) >>> 0; let t = s; t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };\n  f.seed = seed; return f;\n}\nBB.rng = mulberry;\nconst hashStr = s => { let h = 2166136261; for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) { h ^= s.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); } return h >>> 0; };\nBB.hashStr = hashStr;\nBB.RNG = {\n  runSeed: 4141,\n  streams: {},\n  stream(name) { return this.streams[name] || (this.streams[name] = mulberry(hashStr(name) ^ this.runSeed)); },\n  reseed(seed) { this.runSeed = seed >>> 0; this.streams = {}; },\n  /* cosmetic stream: drawing from it never shifts gameplay */\n  fx() { return this.stream('fx'); }\n};\nBB.rand = (a, b, name = 'spawn') => a + (b - a) * BB.RNG.stream(name)();\nBB.fxr = (a = 0, b = 1) => a + (b - a) * BB.RNG.stream('fx')();\nBB.pickFrom = (list, name = 'spawn') => list[Math.floor(BB.RNG.stream(name)() * list.length) % list.length];\n\n/* value noise used by terrain, fog and clouds */\nfunction hash2(ix, iy, seed) { let h = (ix * 374761393 + iy * 668265263 + seed * 2147483647) | 0; h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 1274126177); return ((h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }\nfunction noise2(x, y, seed = 1) {\n  const ix = Math.floor(x), iy = Math.floor(y), fx = x - ix, fy = y - iy;\n  const sx = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx), sy = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy);\n  const a = hash2(ix, iy, seed), b = hash2(ix + 1, iy, seed), c = hash2(ix, iy + 1, seed), d = hash2(ix + 1, iy + 1, seed);\n  return lerp(lerp(a, b, sx), lerp(c, d, sx), sy);\n}\nBB.noise2 = noise2; BB.hash2 = hash2;\n\n/* ---------- tuning (the dev sliders, Appendix A of the plan) ---------- */\nconst TUNING_DEFS = [\n  ['animalSpeed', 'Animal speed', 1, .25, 2, .05], ['spook', 'Gunshot fear', 1, 0, 2, .05], ['doeShare', 'Does and fawns', 1, 0, 2, .1],\n  ['siteTime', 'Site time x', 1, .3, 3, .1], ['reticleSpeed', 'Reticle speed', 330, 150, 900, 10], ['assist', 'Aim assist friction', .65, 0, 1, .05],\n  ['rounds', 'Rounds in tube', 5, 1, 10, 1], ['rackTime', 'Pump time', .22, 0, .6, .02], ['reloadTime', 'Reload time', 1.25, .2, 3, .05],\n  ['scopeMag', 'Scope zoom', 3.5, 1.5, 6, .1], ['sway', 'Scope sway', 2.6, 0, 6, .1], ['breath', 'Hold breath (s)', 3, 1, 6, .25],\n  ['calls', 'Calls per site', 2, 0, 5, 1], ['callFreeze', 'Call freeze (s)', 1.4, 0, 4, .1], ['distanceSlope', 'Metres per +1 dist x', 75, 25, 200, 5],\n  ['heartMult', 'Heart shot x', 2, .5, 4, .1], ['headMult', 'Head shot x', 1.8, .5, 4, .1], ['lungMult', 'Lung shot x', 1.6, .5, 4, .1],\n  ['runningMult', 'Running shot x', 1.25, 1, 2, .05], ['antlerBoost', 'Antler size', 1.15, 1, 2, .05], ['animalScale', 'Animal size', 1.1, .8, 1.6, .05],\n  ['fog', 'Fog', 1, 0, 2, .1], ['timeOfDay', 'Time of day', 0, -1, 1, .1], ['timeScale', 'Game speed', 1, .1, 2, .05]\n];\nBB.TUNING_DEFS = TUNING_DEFS;\nBB.T = {};\nBB.dev = { god: false, infinite: false, freeze: false, slow: false, overlays: { zones: false, labels: false, fps: false }, open: false, page: 0, freecam: false };\nfunction resetTuning() { for (const d of TUNING_DEFS) BB.T[d[0]] = d[2]; }\nresetTuning();\nBB.resetTuning = () => { resetTuning(); saveTuning(); };\nfunction saveTuning() { try { E.store.set('bbho.tuning', BB.T); } catch (e) { /* storage blocked */ } }\nBB.saveTuning = saveTuning;\nBB.loadTuning = () => { const t = E.store.get('bbho.tuning', null); if (t) for (const d of TUNING_DEFS) if (typeof t[d[0]] === 'number') BB.T[d[0]] = clamp(t[d[0]], d[3], d[4]); };\n\n/* ---------- event bus ---------- */\nconst handlers = {};\nBB.bus = {\n  on(n, f) { (handlers[n] || (handlers[n] = [])).push(f); return () => { handlers[n] = handlers[n].filter(h => h !== f); }; },\n  emit(n, d) { const l = handlers[n]; if (l) for (const f of l.slice()) { try { f(d); } catch (e) { if (BB.game) BB.game.fail('event ' + n, e); } } },\n  clear() { for (const k in handlers) delete handlers[k]; }\n};\n\n/* ---------- records (saves) ---------- */\nconst REC_KEY = 'bbho.records';\nBB.defaultRecords = () => ({ stars: {}, best: {}, mounts: {}, plaques: {}, range: false, champion: false, tables: {}, hunts: 0, shots: 0, kills: 0, tutorial: {} });\nBB.records = BB.defaultRecords();\nBB.loadRecords = () => { const r = E.store.get(REC_KEY, null); if (r && typeof r === 'object') BB.records = Object.assign(BB.defaultRecords(), r); };\nBB.saveRecords = () => { try { E.store.set(REC_KEY, BB.records); } catch (e) { /* ignore */ } };\nBB.resetRecords = () => { BB.records = BB.defaultRecords(); BB.saveRecords(); };\nBB.addScore = (table, name, score) => {\n  const t = BB.records.tables[table] || (BB.records.tables[table] = []);\n  t.push({ name, score }); t.sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score); t.length = Math.min(t.length, 8); BB.saveRecords();\n  return t.findIndex(e => e.name === name && e.score === score);\n};\nBB.tablePlaces = (table, score) => { const t = BB.records.tables[table] || []; return t.filter(e => e.score > score).length; };\n\n/* ---------- players' seat colours (AI Hub) and reticle shapes ---------- */\nBB.COLORS = ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'];\nBB.SHAPES = ['circle', 'diamond', 'brackets', 'triangle'];\nBB.COLOR_NAMES = ['RED', 'BLUE', 'GREEN', 'GOLD'];\n\n/* ---------- ui text helpers ---------- */\nBB.txt = (g, s, x, y, c = '#fff', o = {}) => E.font.text(g, s, Math.round(x), Math.round(y), c, Object.assign({ shadow: '#000', outline: false }, o));\nBB.tw = (s, o) => E.font.width(s, o || {});\nBB.fmt = n => String(Math.round(n)).replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, ',');\n\n/* ---------- glyphs: what to show for an action, by the device used last ---------- */\nconst PS = { cross: ['✕', '#7aa7ff'], circle: ['○', '#ff7a7a'], square: ['□', '#ff9ad0'], triangle: ['△', '#7ae0a8'] };\nconst XB = { cross: ['A', '#6fd07a'], circle: ['B', '#ff6a6a'], square: ['X', '#6aa0ff'], triangle: ['Y', '#ffd24a'] };\nconst ACTIONS = {\n  confirm: { pad: 'cross', key: 'Enter', mouse: 'Click' },\n  cancel: { pad: 'circle', key: 'Esc', mouse: 'Esc' },\n  fire: { pad: 'R2', key: 'Space', mouse: 'Click' },\n  pump: { pad: 'square', key: 'R', mouse: 'R / Wheel' },\n  scope: { pad: 'L2', key: 'Q', mouse: 'Right click' },\n  breath: { pad: 'L1', key: 'Shift', mouse: 'Shift' },\n  call: { pad: 'triangle', key: 'E', mouse: 'E' },\n  start: { pad: 'Options', key: 'Enter', mouse: 'Click' },\n  pause: { pad: 'Options', key: 'Esc', mouse: 'Esc' },\n  move: { pad: 'L stick', key: 'WASD', mouse: 'Mouse' },\n  aim: { pad: 'L stick', key: 'WASD', mouse: 'Mouse' },\n  join: { pad: 'Options', key: 'Enter', mouse: 'Click' },\n  tab: { pad: 'L1 R1', key: 'Q E', mouse: 'Q E' },\n  next: { pad: 'R1', key: 'Tab', mouse: 'Tab' }\n};\nBB.ACTIONS = ACTIONS;\nBB.device = () => { const g = BB.game; if (!g) return 'keyboard'; const d = g.input.lastDevice; return d === 'gamepad' ? 'pad' : d === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : d === 'touch' ? 'key' : 'key'; };\nBB.xbox = () => !!(BB.game && BB.game.settings && BB.game.settings.glyphs === 'Xbox');\n/* label for an action under the current device, e.g. ✕ / A / Enter */\nBB.glyphLabel = (act, dev) => {\n  const a = ACTIONS[act] || { pad: act, key: act, mouse: act }; dev = dev || BB.device();\n  if (dev === 'pad') {\n    const p = a.pad; const m = BB.xbox() ? XB : PS;\n    if (m[p]) return m[p][0];\n    if (BB.xbox()) return ({ R2: 'RT', L2: 'LT', L1: 'LB', R1: 'RB', 'L1 R1': 'LB RB', Options: 'Menu' })[p] || p;\n    return p;\n  }\n  return dev === 'mouse' ? a.mouse : a.key;\n};\n/* draws a small button glyph and returns its width */\nBB.glyph = (g, act, x, y, dev) => {\n  dev = dev || BB.device(); const lab = BB.glyphLabel(act, dev); const a = ACTIONS[act] || {};\n  const m = BB.xbox() ? XB : PS; const col = dev === 'pad' && m[a.pad] ? m[a.pad][1] : '#e8e4ff';\n  const w = Math.max(11, BB.tw(lab) + 6);\n  if (dev === 'pad') {\n    const r = 6; E.px.disc(g, x + 6, y + 5, r, '#10131f'); E.px.disc(g, x + 6, y + 5, r - 1, '#242a44');\n    if (m[a.pad]) { drawPadSym(g, a.pad, x + 6, y + 5, col); return 13; }\n    E.px.rect(g, x, y, w, 11, '#10131f'); E.px.rect(g, x + 1, y + 1, w - 2, 9, '#2c3354'); BB.txt(g, lab, x + 3, y + 2, '#fff', { shadow: false }); return w;\n  }\n  E.px.rect(g, x, y, w, 11, '#0b0d16'); E.px.rect(g, x + 1, y + 1, w - 2, 8, '#d9d6ea'); E.px.rect(g, x + 1, y + 9, w - 2, 1, '#8b86a8');\n  BB.txt(g, lab, x + 3, y + 2, '#1a1730', { shadow: false });\n  return w;\n};\nfunction drawPadSym(g, sym, cx, cy, col) {\n  if (BB.xbox()) { const t = XB[sym][0]; BB.txt(g, t, cx - BB.tw(t) / 2 + .5, cy - 3, col, { shadow: false }); return; }\n  const px = E.px;\n  if (sym === 'cross') { px.line(g, cx - 3, cy - 3, cx + 3, cy + 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx - 3, cy + 3, cx + 3, cy - 3, col, 1); }\n  else if (sym === 'circle') { for (let a = 0; a < 16; a++) px.dot(g, Math.round(cx + Math.cos(a / 16 * 6.283) * 3.4), Math.round(cy + Math.sin(a / 16 * 6.283) * 3.4), col); }\n  else if (sym === 'square') { px.line(g, cx - 3, cy - 3, cx + 3, cy - 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx + 3, cy - 3, cx + 3, cy + 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx + 3, cy + 3, cx - 3, cy + 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx - 3, cy + 3, cx - 3, cy - 3, col, 1); }\n  else { px.line(g, cx, cy - 4, cx + 4, cy + 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx + 4, cy + 3, cx - 4, cy + 3, col, 1); px.line(g, cx - 4, cy + 3, cx, cy - 4, col, 1); }\n}\n/* a prompt row: [glyph] LABEL  [glyph] LABEL ... centred or left aligned; items: [[action, label], ...] */\nBB.prompts = (g, items, x, y, align = 'center', dev) => {\n  let total = 0; const parts = items.map(([a, l]) => { const gw = Math.max(13, BB.tw(BB.glyphLabel(a, dev)) + 7); const w = gw + 3 + BB.tw(l); total += w + 10; return [a, l, gw, w]; });\n  total -= 10; let cx = align === 'center' ? x - total / 2 : align === 'right' ? x - total : x;\n  for (const [a, l, gw, w] of parts) { BB.glyph(g, a, Math.round(cx), y, dev); BB.txt(g, l, cx + gw + 3, y + 2, '#e8e4ff'); cx += w + 10; }\n};\n\n/* ---------- audio helper: sfx on an offset (valley echoes) ---------- */\nBB.sfx = (name, o) => { const a = BB.game && BB.game.audio; if (a && !BB.muteSfx) try { a.sfx(name, o); } catch (e) { /* audio blocked */ } };\nBB.sfxLater = (name, delay, o) => { if (BB.game) BB.game.after(delay, () => BB.sfx(name, o)); };\n})();\n"}}}
