{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghx6cDrcxVNs5W2TyzGE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked the build against TASK.md's own feature list. TASK.md was printed in full by my first command (`cat STAGE.md; cat TASK.md`), so the list below is the one it gave. One item is only partly met and I note it at the end.\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Single bundled `.html` with the given file name | `BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-053803.html` is in the work root. It was built by `build/build.mjs` and loads in Chromium with no page errors. |\n| Genre, perspective and a title riffing on the source | First-person arcade hunting shooter titled \"Big Buck Hunt-Off\". I used the plan's title; I did not draw one myself. |\n| Built on the engine; art, animation and audio in code | Engine v0.85.2 unmodified. All art is procedural, the animal rig is new, and all music, sfx and Animalese voices are synthesised. No audio files. |\n| Feature-complete vertical slice | Nine sites, three trophy hunts, three bonus games, a practice range, a lodge, tallies with a shot chart, results with rivals and a ceremony. The `--full` test plays all 15 segments to the lodge. |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset | The pause menu lists \"Dev mode\" (screenshot). It has 24 sliders with per-row and global reset, tools, overlays, a free camera and labs. The test suite covers slider effects, reset and god mode. |\n| Attract mode: 10 s idle on title or menu, looping AI demo, any input exits | Tested for both title and menu. The demo loops a 7-item playlist and survives 160 s. |\n| Multiplayer, local and AI Hub | 1–4 players on one screen, bots fill empty seats. AI Hub ghost mode passed the hub's own conformance harness (`conformance: PASS`). |\n| Narrative tone | Emcee, Uncle Dub, Granny Mae and the rivals, with all-caps barks and Animalese dialog. |\n| 10-foot controller-first UI, prompts follow the last device, Xbox glyph option | Menus use pad, key and mouse hover and click. The glyph helper switches between PlayStation, Xbox and keys. I verified the Xbox setting returns \"A\" and \"RT\". |\n| Touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\", settings button, attract runs | The title shows the message when the touch check is true, with a Settings button. |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | The game sources are clean. The one `placeholder` hit is an engine comment about its own version stamp. |\n| `exit-interview.json` and the four report sections | The file parses with every field filled, and the sections are in my earlier reply. |\n\nOne part is only partly met: the touch-only message was checked in code and in a desktop run, but I never ran the game on a touch-only device.\n\nI did simplify the plan in a few places. The trophy encounters use fewer set-pieces, the critter set is smaller, and the Snowmoose is a scripted event rather than a full fight. All three trophies and all three bonus games are playable and scored. \"Rougher than the plan\" in my earlier note meant visual polish (small animals, blocky ground patches), not missing TASK.md features."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":414500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e576ea7-ae6c-4602-b536-6bfa64a9b891","uuid":"ed5cb31c-ab1d-481e-89b6-5d43346ec24c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:16:20.649Z","request_id":"req_011Cghx6boZUvoFgbf19w97U"}
