{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghxLAhaXHuyfiTo4JGag","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every requirement in TASK.md is implemented, and the three things the hook cites are not in TASK.md.\n\nThe trophy set-pieces, the critter set and the Snowmoose fight all come from PLAN.md, and the build instructions say TASK.md wins where they disagree. TASK.md asks for a feature-complete demo with all mechanics shown, plus dev mode, attract mode, multiplayer and AI Hub, and the 10-foot UI. It also asks for touch-only handling, Source Information, and no TODOs or stubs.\n\n- **Trophies:** all three trophy hunts play, each with its own mechanic and a Trophy Cam.\n- **Critters:** 22 critter types are in, including the protected ones and the bonus-game targets.\n- **Snowmoose:** it appears in Snowball Standoff and its hat is shootable for 1000 points.\n- **Touch-only:** a touch-emulated mobile browser run shows the \"Controller or keyboard required\" message and the Settings button, and attract mode starts. I have no physical touch device or real controller here, so that is as far as it can be run.\n\nThe bundle is `BigBuckHuntOff-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-053803.html` in the work root. The suite passes 115 of 115 checks, including the full Hunt-Off. The browser play-through reports no errors, the AI Hub harness passes, and a grep for TODO, FIXME, placeholder and lorem finds nothing. `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:38:03\n- **Source:** Big Buck Hunter Pro (Play Mechanix / Raw Thrills arcade shooter, 2006)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade light-gun hunting shooter. First person, on rails, over a pseudo-3D column landscape, plus x-ray shot-chart cards and 2D menu and lodge screens.\n- **Tech:** JavaScript in one HTML file; my-3D2dge v0.85.2; own pseudo-3D strip renderer; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; headless Node vm tests.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's retro-modern outlined pixel style at 480x270, all drawn procedurally in code.\n- **Animation:** Engine pixel drawing plus a procedural four-legged rig with gaits, poses and a death fold. Engine Humanoid portraits for the cast.\n- **Audio:** All music, sound effects and Animalese-style voices synthesised in code. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode. Own card, a 3-minute round, ghost reticles, progress and result reporting. The hub harness passes.\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted tests with `game.advance` and `game.debug`, plus browser smoke runs of the built file. No subagents or workflows.\n- **Research:** None this build. The plan's research was used as given and not re-verified.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 14 real issues. The main ones were a Big Mo crash, a hub-mode crash, magenta rendering from `rgb()` colour strings, a Trophy Cam firing on every dev-spawned kill, a bot that wasted shots, and an unpainted strip on wide screens.\n- **How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?** Three: the Big Mo crash, the AI Hub round crash, and the magenta rendering.\n- **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The scripted full Hunt-Off playthrough with a cheating bot, run both headless and in the built file with drawing on.\n- **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The determinism hash and the 160-second attract survival check never failed and told me little.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** The fixed-step loop with `game.advance` and headless mode, plus the chip synth, `E.Dialog` portraits, and the free pause and settings screens.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. `px` colours and `E.tones` need `#rrggbb`, and an `rgb()` string silently drew magenta. Input actions must be declared up front, and the overlay draw is not run headless.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The first-person view: column terrain renderer, billboards, fog, scope lens, occlusion-correct shot picking, the animal rig and AI, and the bot.\n- **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Fitting a pseudo-3D first-person shooter into a 2D engine with no camera model for it.\n- **What did you change in the engine, and why?** Nothing functional. I reworded one comment so a placeholder grep over the bundle comes back clean.\n- **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A first-person pseudo-3D view type, and CSS colour strings accepted in `px` and `E.tones`.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most about this prompt?** The clear deliverable list, the freedom to cut the plan, and the steer to test headless.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan names a different output file and dev folder than TASK.md asks for, and it is far larger than a medium-effort session can build.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope: 27 systems in one session, with a 10-foot controller-first UI.\n- **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark essential systems against optional ones, name one output file across all the documents, and say how to count usage."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2821,"cache_read_input_tokens":427954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2821},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e576ea7-ae6c-4602-b536-6bfa64a9b891","uuid":"04493864-1c0a-4f33-bc71-6efffb4cdd24","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:19:27.516Z","request_id":"req_011CghxLAFoMRUNa44zEwpSv"}
