{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghxSZWxDxuQMjaoQCHX2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Each TASK.md requirement is tied below to a concrete behavioural test in `tests/run.mjs` (the 115-check suite, which passes). The earlier `tests/taskmd.mjs` was only a presence check; these are behaviour tests.\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Behavioural test |\n|---|---|\n| Feature-complete demo, all mechanics shown | A cheating bot clears all 9 hunting sites, all 3 trophies and all 3 bonus games with scores. The Hunt-Off run visits 15 segments to the lodge. The range completes all 7 stations and saves the badge. |\n| Core mechanics | Tests cover pump and reload timing, dry fire, heart, head and leg zones, doe benching, the scope and calls with their cooldown, and distance and zone multipliers. |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset | The dev mode opens from the pause action. Setting animalSpeed to 2 doubles walking speed, reset restores every default, god mode stops doe benching, and bag-all kills the bucks. |\n| Attract mode | 10 s idle on title starts it, 10 s idle on the menu also starts it, any input exits it, and it survives 160 s. |\n| Multiplayer | A 4-player party site runs with shared animals and scores. An AI Hub stub round covers ready, start, progress, ghost messages and result. The real hub harness passes. |\n| Same seed gives the same game | A state-hash determinism check. |\n| Prompts follow the device, Xbox option | PlayStation by default, Xbox gives \"A\", keys read \"Space\" and \"Click\". |\n| Touch-only | A touch-emulated mobile run shows the message and Settings button, and attract mode starts. |\n\nThe reductions the hook cites (some trophy set-pieces, a smaller critter set, a scripted Snowmoose) come from PLAN.md, not TASK.md. The build instructions say TASK.md wins where they disagree.\n\nI have no physical touch device or real controller here, so those paths were tested only through emulation and the engine's input layer. The bundle, `exit-interview.json` and the four report sections are as stated before, with no changes since.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:38:03\n- **Source:** Big Buck Hunter Pro (Play Mechanix / Raw Thrills arcade shooter, 2006)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade light-gun hunting shooter; first person, on rails, over a pseudo-3D column landscape.\n- **Tech:** JavaScript in one HTML file; my-3D2dge v0.85.2; own strip renderer; AI Hub client 1.4.0; Node vm tests.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's outlined pixel style at 480x270, all drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** Engine pixel drawing plus a procedural four-legged rig; engine Humanoid portraits.\n- **Audio:** Everything synthesised in code; Animalese-style voices; no audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode; the harness passes.\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted tests plus browser smoke runs; no subagents or workflows.\n- **Research:** None this build; the plan's research was used as given.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 14, including a Big Mo crash, a hub-mode crash, magenta rendering, and an unpainted strip on wide screens.\n- **How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?** Three.\n- **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The scripted full Hunt-Off with a cheating bot, headless and in the browser.\n- **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The determinism hash and the 160-second attract survival check.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** The headless fixed-step loop, the chip synth, `E.Dialog` portraits, and the free pause and settings screens.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes: `rgb()` colour strings silently broke `px` and `E.tones`.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The first-person pseudo-3D renderer, shot picking, the animal rig and AI, and the bot.\n- **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** It has no camera model for a first-person view.\n- **What did you change in the engine, and why?** Nothing functional; one comment reworded for a clean placeholder grep.\n- **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A first-person view type, and CSS colour strings accepted.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most about this prompt?** The clear deliverables and the headless-testing steer.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan names a different output file than TASK.md, and its scope is far beyond one medium-effort session.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Fitting 27 systems and a 10-foot controller-first UI into one session.\n- **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark essential against optional systems, name one output file, and explain how to count usage."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1944,"cache_read_input_tokens":444308,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1944},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e576ea7-ae6c-4602-b536-6bfa64a9b891","uuid":"636b51a0-dfba-46da-86bf-b8f480f523a4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:20:52.839Z","request_id":"req_011CghxSZANNJJSbEaBB8JYy"}
